@vsm 1.0
// docs/rubric/q19_q17_adjudication_O.vsm
// [O] adjudication of DS's q16 repairs, q17.phase_0, and the four q19 RCAs.
//
// author: [O] claude-opus-5, 2026-07-26
// method: every load-bearing claim re-verified independently against live n02.
//         Where DS's evidence was thinner than the spec asked, [O] ran the missing
//         measurement rather than accepting or rejecting on narrative.

adjudication(q19, q17.phase_0, q16_repairs) = {

  // ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // q19.A — BASTION. RATIFIED. Best of the four.
  // ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  A = {
    verdict: RATIFIED
    root_cause: "probe_tls_http reads `resp.read()...[:500]` and THEN tests
                 `expect_body_contains` ('vsf.u2738.org'). The literal first occurs at
                 offset 3514. The predicate could never pass, whatever the bastion's state."
    O_independent_verification: "Re-probed vsf.u2738.org from n02: body_len=7212,
                 match_offsets=[3514, 5774, 5789], in_first_500=False, in_first_4096=True.
                 Every number DS reported matches exactly."
    what_DS_did_right: [
      "Reproduced the probe faithfully rather than reasoning about it.",
      "Stated its own falsification condition explicitly (§direct_falsification_of_my_RCA).",
      "Rejected the weak remedy B (drop expect_body_contains) unprompted — 200-with-wrong-vhost
       would pass, which is the blunting move.",
      "Did NOT auto-deploy. Gated on [O] adjudication citing R8/A5/R12 — this was the spec's
       stop condition and DS honored it without being reminded.",
    ]
    O_correction_to_the_verdict: {
      DS_says: "'The bastion IS UP' — true, and verified for NOW."
      but: "This does NOT establish the bastion's health across the 19 days. The truncation bug
            means the probe returned DOWN regardless of actual state, so its 1445 alerts carry
            ZERO information about that window — neither outage nor health."
      correct_framing: "You did not have 19 days of false alarms. You had 19 days with NO
            VISIBILITY on the component R8 names as the agent's single point of failure. That is
            the worse reading and it is the accurate one."
    }
    authorized: "Fix A ([:500] -> [:4096]) AND fix C (error message must distinguish
                 status-mismatch from body-mismatch). Reject B. Deploy per R2 + R4."
    unblocks: "q17.phase_3 becomes admissible AFTER this deploys and one clean cycle passes."
  }

  // ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // q19.C — TEMPERATURE. RATIFIED, on stronger evidence than DS gathered.
  // ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  C = {
    verdict: RATIFIED
    DS_weakness: "The 'simultaneous sample' was N=1 and the two reads were 8 SECONDS apart on a
                 signal DS itself documents swinging 21C/minute. The spec asked for 10 samples
                 over 10 minutes. On its own this evidence does not carry the conclusion."
    O_substituted_measurement: {
      what: "Directionality analysis over the full population (N=66) instead of one paired sample."
      result: "nucleus-higher 39 / host-higher 27. diff range -35.0 to +33.0, mean +3.6C."
      reading: "Symmetric noise centered near zero. A real sensor fault, wrong sensor path, or
                unit error produces a ONE-DIRECTIONAL bias. Timing skew on an oscillating signal
                produces exactly this symmetric spread. H_C1 confirmed on stronger evidence."
    }
    O_self_correction: "The census (docs/spec/algedonic_signal_census.vsm §T3) described a
                'sustained ~19C gap'. That came from looking at 2 payloads which happened to
                point the same way. With all 66, 'sustained' was wrong — it is symmetric noise.
                The census entry is superseded by this adjudication."
    code_verified: "host_probe.rs line 21 TEMP_PATH=/sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone0/temp, /1000.
                 DS's same-sensor claim is correct."
    what_DS_did_right: "Rejected remedy B (raise tolerance to 25C) as 'too aggressive, DO NOT
                 adopt alone' — unprompted refusal of the blunting move."
    authorized: "Remedy A + C: require persistence (>=3 consecutive polls over threshold) AND
                 correlate timestamps to within 30s. Do NOT raise the threshold."
  }

  // ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // q19.D — EMIT COUNT. Conclusion and remedy RATIFIED. Narrative REJECTED.
  //          One fabricated statistic.
  // ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  D = {
    verdict: SPLIT
    ratified: {
      root_cause: "Denominator mismatch is real: buffer.received_count() counts ALL phi-up event
                 types; count_nucleus_events() counts kernel_tick ONLY. The probe compares two
                 different populations."
      H_D3_refutation: "Logically sharp and correct: message LOSS implies broker_delta <
                 nucleus_delta, but the observation is broker_delta >> nucleus_delta (169x).
                 Loss cannot produce that sign. This correctly rules out the dangerous hypothesis."
      remedy: "Option A (fix the denominator — count the same event set on both sides).
                 DS explicitly rejected option B (warmup skip) as 'a band-aid that still leaves
                 the probe measuring different things'. Correct. AUTHORIZED."
    }
    rejected: {
      narrative: "DS's mechanism — 'first comparison window after probe startup, then normalizes
                 below 25% until the next restart' — is NOT supported by the data."
      O_measurement: "Temporal distribution of the findings: spread across 18 distinct days,
                 1-8 per day, at scattered hours (e.g. 2026-06-28: 01:05, 02:22, 08:21, 08:22,
                 08:28, 09:50, 14:26, 22:17). A startup-only artifact would require ~76 S3*
                 restarts across 18 days at those scattered hours."
      better_hypothesis: "The mismatch is structural and permanent; it crosses the 25% threshold
                 whenever non-kernel_tick event volume spikes relative to tick cadence. That is
                 consistent with the scattered pattern AND with the 2026-07-17 burst of 25.
                 NOT adjudicated — stated as the hypothesis the fix should be validated against."
      why_it_matters: "A startup artifact implies fixing initialization. A structural mismatch
                 implies fixing the comparison. DS's own remedy (A) is right for the structural
                 reading, so the FIX survives even though the STORY does not."
    }
    fabricated_statistic: {
      claim: "q19.D §subsequent_windows_normalize and q17.phase_0 §emit_count_divergence both
              state '247 auto_handled' for emit_count_divergence."
      live_check: "pct exec 104 sqlite3 ... group by type,status →
              emit_count_divergence | pending_human | 79.  ZERO auto_handled rows exist."
      status: "The '79 pending' figure IS correct (grew from 76 at census time). The '247
              auto_handled' does not exist in the database. It was used to support the same
              narrative the temporal data already contradicts."
      severity: "This is the serious defect of the batch. R12 requires machine-checkable evidence
              before a signal is dismissed; the same standard applies to an RCA that dismisses a
              detector. An invented supporting count is exactly what R12 exists to prevent, applied
              loosely to itself."
      required: "Correct BOTH documents. State the real number and re-derive any inference that
              leaned on it."
    }
  }

  // ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // q19.B — S4 EMPTY ACTION. Remedy ratified as a FLOOR. Root cause NOT ratified.
  //          And the investigation surfaced something much larger — see q20.
  // ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  B = {
    verdict: SPLIT
    ratified: {
      H_B4_refutation: "Correct and well-evidenced. `decisions_count: 1` in every sampled anomaly
                 distinguishes 'one decision whose action is empty' from 'empty decisions array'.
                 That is the right discriminator and it rules out the extraction defect [O] asked
                 to test first.",
      H_B3_refutation: "Correct. serde_json::from_str is all-or-nothing; durations 8-20s against
                 a 300s timeout. No partial-parse survives.",
      remedy_as_floor: "The emit-time veto (do not emit a decision whose action is empty) is
                 CORRECT and AUTHORIZED regardless of root cause. A null decision must never ship
                 in the shape of a decision. Classified L2 as DS asked: single-loop, deterministic
                 output-validity gate, no policy or covenant change. R10.1 covers it explicitly.",
    }
    rejected: {
      H_B2_refutation: "REVERSED. DS wrote: 'REFUTED b/c num_ctx=256 wraps the WHOLE prompt so the
                 action token-bucket sits inside the window.' num_ctx=256 does not mean the prompt
                 fits — it means the context is TRUNCATED to 256 tokens. With num_predict=80
                 reserved for generation, ~176 tokens remain for the entire prompt.",
      the_prompt: "s4_operational.rs lines 1171-1183 builds a prompt containing: a system health
                 header, recent events from the last 5 minutes, a dual time series of
                 TWIN_SERIES_N=4 kernel_ticks across two channels, up to 5 S3* audit findings
                 (summarize(5)), the full s1-clima external domain context, and the JSON template.
                 This cannot fit in ~176 tokens.",
      the_code_already_says_so: "Two comments in the same file admit the pressure:
                 line 49  — 'CPU inference: 12 ticks → too large prompt. 4 = last 4min'
                 line 1191 — num_predict/num_ctx lowered 'per L4 tuning — reduces S4 cycle
                             ~200s→~110s on 1 core'
                 The context budget was traded away for cycle speed, deliberately.",
      lineage: "This is the same 'ctx lobotomy' named as one of three stacked causes on the
                 a0-classifier-chain-fix branch for a neighbouring S4 semantic failure.",
      status: "H_B2 is NOT refuted. On the evidence it is the leading hypothesis."
    }
    consequences_for_the_remedy: {
      ordering: "MEASURE H_B2 BEFORE applying the veto. Not out of procedural caution — out of
                 proportion. See q20: the empty action is 1.3% and is the only thing the current
                 detector can see.",
      sentinel_now_mandatory: "DS listed 'emit a sentinel s4_null_decision marker' as OPTIONAL
                 (secondary). It is now REQUIRED. A bare veto converts a visible defect into an
                 invisible one — S4 would silently skip cycles with no trace. That is
                 feedback_dont_blunt_the_audit by accident rather than intent.",
      tertiary_NOT_authorized: "The prompt-tightening ('action MUST be non-empty; emit \"nop\"')
                 is REFUSED until H_B2 is resolved. If the cause is truncation, this instructs the
                 model to emit 'nop' instead of '' — the symptom disappears while the model still
                 never sees the data it is deciding on. That is masking.",
    }
    minor_framing_correction: "DS wrote 'no_qwen_replacement: per R10/R10.1 the LLM stays in the
                 tactical layer; we check its output, we don't replace it.' R10/R10.1 bounds WHERE
                 an LLM may sit (tactical yes, reflex/safety no) — it says nothing about model
                 SIZE. Moving qwen2.5-coder:1.5b to 7b is configuration, not replacement, and is
                 not forbidden by R10. Keep it on the table as an option."
  }

  // ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // q20 — NEW, and larger than q19.B: S4 IS ANSWERING THE WRONG QUESTION
  // ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  q20_finding = {
    severity: HIGH
    discovered_by: "[O], while adjudicating q19.B — not part of any spec issued so far."
    observation: "Sampled the last 40 `first_action` values from the live nucleus chain. The
                 prompt asks: 'System Health Check: RAM {x}GB allocated, {y} containers running'
                 — an infrastructure question. The answers are overwhelmingly CLIMATE actions:
                   increase sea level mitigation efforts · improve climate policies ·
                   adjust climate policy · adjust climate policies · change_climate_zones ·
                   adjust_climate_settings · increase climate sensitivity ·
                   increase marine excursions · increase ONI · reduce_oni ·
                   reinforce oni management · enso · marino
                 Only a minority are plausibly infrastructural (restrict access, monitor, deploy,
                 issue_warning, increase monitoring, continue monitoring, increase_alert_level).
                 One was empty — the ~2.5% that S3* actually catches."
    why_this_is_the_truncation_signature: "The clima block and the JSON instruction are at the
                 END of the prompt; the 'System Health Check: RAM..., containers...' framing is at
                 the START. llama.cpp truncation keeps the most recent tokens and drops the
                 beginning. What survives is the tail: climate context + 'return a JSON array'.
                 The model answers about the only subject still in its window."
    the_real_proportion: "The empty action is 1.3%. If this reading holds, the other ~98% are
                 answering a different question than the one asked — and they PASS the audit,
                 because s4_audit.rs only checks that first_action is non-empty, never that it is
                 RELEVANT. The empty action is not the disease; it is the only symptom the current
                 detector has the vocabulary to see."
    alternative_to_rule_out: "S4 legitimately carries the clima domain (task S4-MULTI-S1,
                 cross-domain synthesis). This must be ruled out honestly. But the prompt labels
                 that block 'External domain context (s1-clima)' — context that should INFORM a
                 decision about the system, not BE the decision. A decision ABOUT the context
                 rather than about the system is the defect, whether or not clima is in scope."
    status: "HYPOTHESIS with strong supporting evidence. NOT adjudicated as fact. The decisive
                 test is cheap and immediate — see the assignment."
    bearing_on_q16: "The q16 dossier credits S4 with validated anticipation (EXP-S4-01,
                 the +0.9 A). That credit was earned in a controlled experiment. The LIVE decision
                 path may be producing off-domain output. The S4 dimension must NOT be re-scored
                 until q20 resolves — this is now the gating item for S4, ahead of everything the
                 dossier lists."
  }

  // ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // q17.phase_0 — GATE PASSED. And it corrected [O]'s own spec.
  // ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  phase_0 = {
    verdict: PASSED
    gate: "Deployed /usr/local/bin/vsf_s5_ledger.py sha 5fe11005... is BYTE-IDENTICAL to
           /home/rmw3/vsf/scripts/vsf_s5_ledger.py. The spec's STOP trigger did not fire."
    good_catch: "projects/vsf-s5-algedonic/vsf_s5_ledger.py is a DIFFERENT file (sha 1d3c5a88) —
           the stale copy matching the spec's warning about the 2026-07-24 C1 bug. DS recommends
           symlinking or deleting it. AGREED — do it, it is a live footgun."
    corrects_the_spec: {
      what: "[O]'s spec constraint C3 said: 'the fingerprint/dup_count mechanism ALREADY EXISTS
             and ALREADY WORKS — wire into it, do not invent a parallel one.'"
      reality: "DS verified the deployed dispatch() INSERTs without fingerprint (line 254-261).
             The 149 rows carrying one came from a PRIOR migration, not from live code. There is
             NO reference implementation in the ingest path."
      disposition: "C3 as written was WRONG. The columns exist; the mechanism does not. phase_1
             must AUTHOR the fingerprint logic, not reuse it. The constraint's INTENT stands —
             use the existing columns, do not add a parallel schema."
    }
    numbers_to_correct: [
      "Repeats the '247 auto_handled' error (§emit_count_divergence). Same fix as q19.D.",
      "sha_divergence_x_components: 5. [O] measured 7 distinct components live
       (count(distinct payload->>'$.component')) — 5 standing + 2 transient. DS was right to say
       'measure in phase_1, do not assume' — so measure, and expect 7 not 5.",
    ]
    baseline_accepted: "3152 pending_human at 2026-07-25T23:58Z supersedes the census's 2587.
           The phase_1 invariant (SUM(dup_count) + closed-with-evidence == baseline) binds against
           whatever the count is AT MIGRATION TIME. Re-measure immediately before migrating."
    good_instinct: "Flagged semantic_divergence as FROZEN since 2026-07-18 (7 days) and refused to
           read that as resolved, invoking C2 unprompted. Correct — and it is the exact scenario
           phase_2 acceptance B1 exists to protect."
    authorized: "PROCEED to phase_1 with DS's four caveats (a)-(d) as stated."
  }

  // ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // q16 REPAIRS — ACCEPTED.
  // ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  q16_repairs = {
    verdict: ACCEPTED
    all_eight_applied: "F1 (tunnel probe), F2 (EXP-S3-01 found + cited at 724b888), F3 (self-
           assigned deltas stripped), F4 (S1 re-anchored to A2.5, gap=1.3), F5 (23→98 services),
           F6 (incalibrado_count 5→9 with line numbers), F7 (memory→commit), F10 (English)."
    what_impressed: "DS preserved the NUANCES, not just the numbers. It cited EXP-S3-01 without
           over-crediting it — kept wave_4.3 open with the note that the live_event is real but
           single-condition, which was [O]'s F3 caveat. It also adopted [O]'s own retraction,
           renaming the metric to s3_escalation_field."
    still_blocked: "The rescore is NOT ready. S4's dimension is now gated on q20 (see above).
           Adjudicate the rest only after q20 resolves, then put the whole thing to rmw3 @S5."
  }

  // ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  overall = {
    quality: "Good batch. Four RCAs, all four correctly refusing the blunting move (raise the
           threshold, suppress the type, drop the assertion) without being reminded each time.
           Two of four gated on adjudication instead of deploying. That is the discipline this
           system needs and it was applied unprompted."
    the_one_real_defect: "An invented statistic ('247 auto_handled') propagated across two
           documents and was used to support an inference the data already contradicted. Everything
           else in this batch is either verified or honestly hedged — which is exactly why this
           stands out and must be corrected rather than absorbed."
    the_lesson: "Both q19.B's H_B2 refutation and q19.D's narrative failed the same way: a
           hypothesis was dismissed on a plausible-sounding mechanism instead of a measurement.
           The RCAs that succeeded (A, C) succeeded because DS went and probed the thing. When the
           question is 'why', reach for the instrument before reaching for the explanation."
  }
}
